                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is GST applicable on hospital services in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Core healthcare by clinical establishments is EXEMPT under Notification 12/2017 Sl.74 (OPD, IPD, surgeries, diagnostics by hospital). Room rent above Rs 5,000/day non-ICU attracts 5% GST without ITC. Pharmacy retail to outpatients, canteen to non-patients, and cosmetic procedures attract GST. Patron segregates exempt and taxable.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is trust audit mandatory for charitable hospitals?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Under S.12A(1)(b), every trust with income exceeding Rs 2,50,000 (before S.11/12) must get CA audit. Form 10B (income > Rs 5 Cr or foreign) or 10BB before ITR-7 due date. Non-filing = loss of entire exemption. Plus Charity Commissioner IX-C and S.41AA bed report.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does healthcare accounting cost in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Clinic/doctor: Rs 15,000-25,000/month. Nursing home (<50 beds): Rs 25,000-50,000. Multi-specialty (50-300 beds): Rs 50,000-1,50,000. Charitable trust: Rs 40,000-1,00,000. Diagnostic lab/pharmacy chain: Rs 15,000-40,000.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can hospitals claim ITC on medical equipment?</h3>
